iness with a $16.5B market cap on $2.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +69% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +63.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -37% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $684M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 31 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.30\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 16% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 116% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.1578454889072052},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Communication Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $36.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Communication Services ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"t